LOK: a size at a bare cursor sets every script to it

With no selection, Writer gives the chosen height to the input
language's script and scales the other scripts by their standard sizes
for the paragraph's languages (zh-CN: Western 12pt, Asian 10.5pt).
Under LOK the input language is the worker host's keyboard, not the
user's: on a host with a Chinese keyboard 14 on an empty line set
Asian 14 and Western 16, the state showed 16 and ElyDoc undid the
change (GitHub ElyOffice #62); on an English one Chinese typed after
came out at 12.25pt. LOK now follows Word: one size for every script.

--- a/sw/source/uibase/shells/basesh.cxx
+++ b/sw/source/uibase/shells/basesh.cxx
@@ -2519,6 +2519,9 @@
                         break;
                         default: break;
                     }
+                    // LOK as Word: one size for every script.
+                    if (comphelper::LibreOfficeKit::isActive())
+                        nWesternSize = nCJKSize = nCTLSize = static_cast<sal_Int32>(nHeight);
                     aHeightSet.Put( SvxFontHeightItem( static_cast<sal_uInt32>(nWesternSize), 100, RES_CHRATR_FONTSIZE ));
                     aHeightSet.Put( SvxFontHeightItem( static_cast<sal_uInt32>(nCJKSize), 100, RES_CHRATR_CJK_FONTSIZE ));
                     aHeightSet.Put( SvxFontHeightItem( static_cast<sal_uInt32>(nCTLSize), 100, RES_CHRATR_CTL_FONTSIZE ));
